   _Assigned_chem_shift_list.Details
;
The NZ atom of LYS 48 in chain A is covalently linked through an isopeptide bond to chain B. 
As a result of this linkage, the side-chain NH3 group of LYS 48 lost two hydrogens and got 
transformed into an amide group (NH). 
This is why the observed NZ chemical shift is consistent with a typical chemical shift of 
an amide nitrogen. 
This also means that the NZ atom has only one hydrogen (HZ) attached to it.
;
